  <data name="HomePage_QuickStart_Content.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Click on Files in the left navigation menu, then click the "Add drive" button to log in to OneDrive. Double click to enter your drive.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_QuickStart_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quick start</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Welcome to SimpleList</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Tutorial_Subtitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connect OneDrive, Google Drive, a local folder, or PikPak from one place. Read the provider notes below before adding your first drive.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_QuickStart_Step1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Complete any provider-specific preparation below. Google Drive requires OAuth credentials before it can be used.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_QuickStart_Step2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Open Drives, select Add drive, choose a provider, and complete sign-in or folder selection.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_QuickStart_Step3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Double-click the new drive to browse files. Use the context menu for upload, download, rename, delete, sharing, and other supported actions.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_OpenDrives.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open Drives</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleNotice.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Google Drive requires configuration</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleNotice.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable the Google Drive API and add a Desktop OAuth Client ID and Client Secret to appsettings.json before signing in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_OneDrive_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>OneDrive</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_OneDrive_Content.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No additional configuration is normally required. Select OneDrive and sign in through the Microsoft browser window. OneDrive supports uploads, downloads, trash, public links, link passwords, and expiration dates.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleDrive_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Google Drive</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleDrive_Prerequisites.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In Google Cloud Console: create or select a project, enable Google Drive API, configure the OAuth consent screen, and create OAuth credentials of type Desktop app. Copy both the Client ID and Client Secret.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_ConfigPath_Label.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create or edit this configuration file:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleDrive_ConfigIntro.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Add the following JSON. If appsettings.json already contains other settings, merge the GoogleOAuth section instead of replacing the whole file.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleDrive_Restart.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Save the file and restart SimpleList before adding Google Drive. The first sign-in opens a browser; the resulting token is cached locally.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_GoogleDrive_Limitations.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Google Drive public links do not support passwords or expiration dates. PDF conversion is limited to native Google Docs, Sheets, and Slides. Resuming an upload starts a new Google upload session.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Local_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Local folder</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_Local_Content.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No account or API configuration is required. Select Local, choose a folder, and grant access when Windows asks. Operations modify the selected folder directly; cloud trash, share links, and PDF conversion are unavailable.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_PikPak_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>PikPak</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_PikPak_Content.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter your PikPak username and password when adding the drive. Sign-in may open a browser-based CAPTCHA challenge. Enable Remember account and password only on a trusted computer.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_PikPak_Limitations.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Some PikPak operations are not available yet</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HomePage_PikPak_Limitations.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Uploading files or folders, creating or revoking share links, PDF conversion, and migrations whose destination is PikPak are currently unsupported.</value>
  </data>
